div.p:
7. He asks that Philemon would receive Onesimus. How? "Not as a servant, but above  a servant."[A] How much above? Philemon was to receive him as "a son" of the apostle--"as a brother beloved"--nay, if he counted Paul a partner, an equal, he was to receive Onesimus as he would receive the apostle himself[
                  B
                  ]. So much  above a servant was he to receive him!

